from (values
('113.51.c.6.B',3,'Shirley Chisholm is known as the first Black woman to do what?','["Win a Nobel Prize", "Command a ship", "Be elected to the U.S. Congress", "Fly a plane"]'::jsonb,2,'She also ran for president in 1972.','original'),
('113.51.c.6.B',3,'Fannie Lou Hamer is remembered for doing what?','["Founding Ebony", "Winning boxing titles", "Flying planes", "Fighting for voting rights in Mississippi"]'::jsonb,3,'She co-founded the Mississippi Freedom Democratic Party.','original'),
('113.51.c.6.C',3,'Since 1970, a notable change in the African American community has been what?','["Growth in college attendance and Black elected officials", "A ban on voting", "Elimination of all inequality", "A halt in migration"]'::jsonb,0,'Progress coexists with challenges.','original'),
('113.51.c.6.C',3,'A continuing challenge since 1970 is the gap in what?','["Hair length", "Household wealth between Black and white families", "Eye color", "Shoe size"]'::jsonb,1,'The racial wealth gap persists.','original'),
('113.51.c.7.A',3,'Which is an example of forced migration in African American history?','["The move to college", "The Great Migration", "The Atlantic slave trade", "Retirement"]'::jsonb,2,'The Great Migration was voluntary.','original'),
('113.51.c.7.A',3,'Which is an example of voluntary migration?','["Slave auctions", "Convict leasing", "The Middle Passage", "The Great Migration to Northern cities"]'::jsonb,3,'People chose to move for opportunity.','original'),
('113.51.c.7.B',3,'Which geographic factor helped the plantation system grow in the South?','["A warm climate and fertile soil for cotton, tobacco and rice", "Arctic cold", "Desert", "Mountains"]'::jsonb,0,'Geography shaped the economy.','original'),
('113.51.c.7.B',3,'Northern textile mills depended on the South because they did what?','["Grew rice", "Processed cotton grown by enslaved labor", "Mined coal only", "Sold machines to Africa"]'::jsonb,1,'The regions'' economies were interdependent.','original'),
('113.51.c.7.C',3,'The Exodusters were African Americans who moved to which state in the late 1870s?','["Florida", "Hawaii", "Kansas", "Maine"]'::jsonb,2,'They sought land and freedom.','original'),
('113.51.c.7.C',3,'The Great Migration changed Northern cities by doing what?','["Ending industry", "Emptying them", "Reducing diversity", "Increasing Black populations and political influence"]'::jsonb,3,'Cities such as Chicago grew.','original'),
('113.51.c.7.D',3,'Urban renewal and highway construction often affected Black neighborhoods by doing what?','["Displacing residents and dividing communities", "Building schools", "Ending segregation", "Increasing property values for all"]'::jsonb,0,'Many Black neighborhoods were cut apart.','original'),
('113.51.c.7.D',3,'The 1927 Mississippi River flood contributed to Black migration because it did what?','["Ended sharecropping", "Destroyed farms and pushed families north", "Created new farms", "Raised wages"]'::jsonb,1,'It displaced many tenant farmers.','original'),
('113.51.c.8.A',3,'The cotton gin (1793) increased demand for enslaved labor because it did what?','["Made cotton worthless", "Ended plantations", "Made cotton much more profitable to grow", "Replaced all workers"]'::jsonb,2,'Eli Whitney invented it.','original'),
('113.51.c.8.A',3,'"King Cotton" refers to what?','["A sports team", "A card game", "A British monarch", "The central role of cotton in the economy of the South and the world"]'::jsonb,3,'Cotton was the top export.','original'),
('113.51.c.8.B',3,'Sharecropping trapped many Black farmers in what?','["A cycle of debt to landowners", "Free land", "Wealth", "Higher wages"]'::jsonb,0,'Crop shares barely covered costs.','original'),
('113.51.c.8.B',3,'Redlining limited economic opportunity by doing what?','["Building schools", "Denying loans and insurance to residents of Black neighborhoods", "Increasing home values", "Raising wages"]'::jsonb,1,'It blocked homeownership and wealth building.','original'),
('113.51.c.8.C',3,'Which factors contributed to the Great Migration?','["Free land in Africa", "Equal rights in the South", "Poor wages, racist violence and jobs in Northern factories", "High Southern wages"]'::jsonb,2,'Push and pull factors drove movement.','original'),
('113.51.c.8.C',3,'The boll weevil contributed to migration by doing what?','["Raising cotton prices", "Ending segregation", "Creating jobs", "Destroying cotton crops and farm income"]'::jsonb,3,'It devastated Southern agriculture.','original'),
('113.51.c.8.D',3,'The Brotherhood of Sleeping Car Porters, led by A. Philip Randolph, was significant because it did what?','["Became the first Black-led union to win a contract with a major company", "Founded the NAACP", "Ended Jim Crow", "Created Social Security"]'::jsonb,0,'It organized Pullman porters.','original'),
('113.51.c.8.D',3,'Many unions in the early 1900s hurt Black workers by doing what?','["Hiring them first", "Excluding them from membership", "Paying them more", "Teaching them for free"]'::jsonb,1,'Exclusion limited access to skilled jobs.','original'),
('113.51.c.8.E',3,'Which factor can influence economic mobility?','["Birthday month", "Favorite color", "Family wealth and educational opportunity", "Shoe size"]'::jsonb,2,'These affect opportunities.','original'),
('113.51.c.8.E',3,'Colorism refers to what?','["A music style", "A type of paint", "A farming method", "Discrimination based on skin tone within and across groups"]'::jsonb,3,'Skin tone has affected opportunity.','original'),
('113.51.c.8.F',3,'Buy Black campaigns and boycotts are examples of what?','["Economic approaches to address inequality", "Military tactics", "School subjects", "Voting methods"]'::jsonb,0,'They use spending power.','original'),
('113.51.c.8.F',3,'Black-owned banks and insurance companies helped communities by doing what?','["Raising taxes", "Providing credit and services when others refused", "Printing newspapers", "Closing neighborhoods"]'::jsonb,1,'They filled gaps left by discrimination.','original'),
('113.51.c.8.G',3,'Madam C. J. Walker built a business empire in what industry?','["Railroads", "Steel", "Hair care and beauty products", "Oil"]'::jsonb,2,'She became one of the first self-made female millionaires.','original'),
('113.51.c.8.G',3,'Johnson Publishing Company, founded by John H. Johnson, produced which magazines?','["Time and Life", "Wired and Mad", "Vogue and Elle", "Ebony and Jet"]'::jsonb,3,'They celebrated Black life.','original'),
('113.51.c.8.H',3,'Black Wall Street was the nickname for a thriving business district in what city?','["Tulsa, Oklahoma", "Denver, Colorado", "Houston, Texas", "Boston, Massachusetts"]'::jsonb,0,'The Greenwood district was destroyed in 1921.','original'),
('113.51.c.8.H',3,'Garrett Morgan is known for inventing what?','["The telephone", "An early traffic signal and a safety hood", "The airplane", "The light bulb"]'::jsonb,1,'His inventions improved safety.','original'),
('113.51.c.9.A',3,'Free Black people in the late 1700s petitioned for freedom by citing what?','["The Bill of Rights", "The Articles of Confederation", "The Declaration of Independence''s claim that all men are created equal", "The Monroe Doctrine"]'::jsonb,2,'They used its ideals to challenge slavery.','original'),
('113.51.c.9.A',3,'Benjamin Banneker wrote to Thomas Jefferson to do what?','["Request a government job", "Ask for money", "Offer him land", "Urge him to see Black people as equals and end slavery"]'::jsonb,3,'He challenged Jefferson''s views.','original'),
('113.51.c.9.B',3,'Before 1877, which region generally gave Black men more voting rights?','["Some Northern states", "The Deep South", "The Confederacy", "Texas"]'::jsonb,0,'Rights varied widely by region.','original'),
('113.51.c.9.B',3,'The Seneca Falls Convention of 1848 addressed the rights of whom?','["Immigrants only", "Women", "Soldiers only", "Farmers only"]'::jsonb,1,'Black abolitionists such as Frederick Douglass attended.','original'),
('113.51.c.9.C',3,'The 15th Amendment prohibited denial of the vote based on what?','["Age", "Property", "Race, color or previous servitude", "Gender"]'::jsonb,2,'It was ratified in 1870.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Social Studies' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
insert into public.question_bank (teks_code, teks_item_id, subject, grade_num, course, difficulty, qtype, prompt, choices, answer_idx, explanation, source, status, gen_batch)
select distinct on (v.prompt) v.code, i.id, d.subject,
       case when i.grade_level = 'K' then 0 when i.grade_level ~ '^[0-9]+' then substring(i.grade_level from '^[0-9]+')::smallint end,
       case when i.grade_level is null then i.grade_course_title end,
       v.diff, 'mc', v.prompt, v.choices, v.ans, v.expl, v.src, 'checked', 'hs_aas_v1'
from (values
('113.51.c.9.D',3,'Smith v. Allwright (1944), a Texas case, ended what practice?','["Convict leasing", "Poll taxes", "School segregation", "The all-white Democratic primary"]'::jsonb,3,'The Court ruled it unconstitutional.','original'),
('113.51.c.9.D',3,'During the 1920s-1950s, anti-lynching bills in Congress were what?','["Repeatedly blocked by Southern senators", "Signed in 1925", "Quickly passed", "Never proposed"]'::jsonb,0,'Federal law did not pass until much later.','original'),
('113.51.c.9.E',3,'The Fair Housing Act of 1968 prohibited what?','["Poll taxes", "Discrimination in the sale and rental of housing", "School prayer", "Segregated buses"]'::jsonb,1,'It was passed after King''s assassination.','original'),
('113.51.c.9.E',3,'Affirmative action policies aimed to do what?','["End voting", "Ban hiring", "Increase opportunities for underrepresented groups in education and employment", "Remove all admissions"]'::jsonb,2,'They remain debated.','original'),
('113.51.c.9.F',3,'In Shelby County v. Holder (2013), the Supreme Court did what?','["Ended segregation", "Legalized slavery", "Created the NAACP", "Struck down a key formula in the Voting Rights Act"]'::jsonb,3,'It limited preclearance requirements.','original'),
('113.51.c.9.F',3,'Changes in the political environment affect civil rights because they do what?','["Influence which laws are passed, enforced or struck down", "Stop elections", "End court cases", "Make laws permanent"]'::jsonb,0,'Policy shifts matter.','original'),
('113.51.c.10.A',3,'The Freedom Riders of 1961 did what?','["Led a farm strike", "Rode interstate buses to challenge segregation in the South", "Flew planes", "Founded the NAACP"]'::jsonb,1,'Black and white riders traveled together.','original'),
('113.51.c.10.A',3,'The 1968 Memphis sanitation workers'' strike connected civil rights and what?','["Space exploration", "Foreign trade", "Labor rights and economic justice", "Sports"]'::jsonb,2,'Dr. King was there when he was assassinated.','original'),
('113.51.c.10.B',3,'Martin Luther King Jr. promoted which philosophy?','["Armed rebellion", "Secession", "Isolation", "Nonviolent resistance"]'::jsonb,3,'He was influenced by Gandhi.','original'),
('113.51.c.10.B',3,'Black Power in the late 1960s emphasized what?','["Racial pride, self-determination and community control", "Assimilation only", "Colonial rule", "Separation by law"]'::jsonb,0,'It energized a new generation.','original'),
('113.51.c.10.C',3,'Hiram Revels was the first African American to do what?','["Win a Nobel Prize", "Serve in the U.S. Senate", "Command an army", "Be elected President"]'::jsonb,1,'He represented Mississippi in 1870.','original'),
('113.51.c.10.C',3,'Barbara Jordan was a Texan who was elected to what?','["The Presidency", "The Senate of Texas only", "The U.S. House of Representatives", "The Supreme Court"]'::jsonb,2,'She was a powerful speaker during the Watergate hearings.','original'),
('113.51.c.11.A',3,'The Dred Scott decision (1857) held that what?','["Black people were citizens", "Slavery was illegal", "Slaves could vote", "Black people were not U.S. citizens and had no rights the government must respect"]'::jsonb,3,'It was later overturned by the 14th Amendment.','original'),
('113.51.c.11.A',3,'The 14th Amendment changed the status of African Americans by doing what?','["Granting citizenship and equal protection", "Abolishing taxes", "Ending the Civil War", "Giving land"]'::jsonb,0,'It overturned Dred Scott.','original'),
('113.51.c.11.B',3,'Regional differences shaped political perspectives because Black communities in the North and South did what?','["Lived in the same conditions", "Faced different laws, opportunities and risks", "Never communicated", "Had identical experiences"]'::jsonb,1,'Context shaped strategies.','original'),
('113.51.c.11.B',3,'Rural Southern communities and Northern urban communities often differed in what?','["Time zones", "Language", "Access to voting, jobs and organizations", "Weather"]'::jsonb,2,'These differences influenced politics.','original'),
('113.51.c.11.C',3,'The term "Negro" was widely used until which period?','["The 2020s", "The 1500s", "The 1700s", "The 1960s"]'::jsonb,3,'"Black" gained popularity with the Black Power movement.','original'),
('113.51.c.11.C',3,'The term "African American" gained popularity in the 1980s, in part through whom?','["Civil rights leader Jesse Jackson", "W. E. B. Du Bois", "Booker T. Washington", "Harriet Tubman"]'::jsonb,0,'It emphasized heritage.','original'),
('113.51.c.11.D',3,'A contemporary issue that has led to diverse viewpoints in public discourse is what?','["Plate tectonics", "Policing and criminal justice reform", "Photosynthesis", "Gravity"]'::jsonb,1,'People discuss it with different perspectives.','original'),
('113.51.c.11.D',3,'Activism today often uses which tools?','["Only pamphlets", "Only telegrams", "Social media, protests and voting drives", "Only newspapers"]'::jsonb,2,'Technology has changed activism.','original'),
('113.51.c.11.E',3,'Afro-Latinos are people who do what?','["Come only from Asia", "Come only from Europe", "Have no ancestry", "Have African ancestry and Latin American heritage"]'::jsonb,3,'Examples include Afro-Cubans and Afro-Brazilians.','original'),
('113.51.c.11.E',3,'The African American community also includes what group?','["Recent immigrants from Africa and the Caribbean", "Only city residents", "Only descendants of enslaved people", "Only Southerners"]'::jsonb,0,'Black America is diverse.','original'),
('113.51.c.12.A',3,'De facto segregation is segregation that occurs because of what?','["Constitutional rules", "Social customs and housing patterns, not law", "Court orders", "Treaties"]'::jsonb,1,'De jure segregation was created by law.','original'),
('113.51.c.12.A',3,'Stereotypes harm African Americans by doing what?','["Creating wealth", "Ending bias", "Limiting opportunities based on false generalizations", "Improving schools"]'::jsonb,2,'They shape discrimination.','original'),
('113.51.c.12.B',3,'African Americans retained cultural identity while adapting by doing what?','["Forbidding change", "Abandoning all traditions", "Isolating from society", "Blending African heritage with American traditions in music, food and religion"]'::jsonb,3,'Gullah Geechee culture is an example.','original'),
('113.51.c.12.B',3,'Gullah Geechee communities of the Southeast preserved what?','["African-influenced language, crafts and food traditions", "Viking runes", "Roman customs", "Spanish law"]'::jsonb,0,'They live along the coast and Sea Islands.','original'),
('113.51.c.12.C',3,'Juneteenth commemorates what?','["The Civil War start", "The announcement of freedom to enslaved people in Texas in 1865", "The Declaration of Independence", "The 15th Amendment"]'::jsonb,1,'It is celebrated June 19.','original'),
('113.51.c.12.C',3,'HBCU traditions such as homecoming and marching bands contribute to what?','["Isolation", "Segregation law", "A strong shared cultural identity", "Disunity"]'::jsonb,2,'They carry community pride.','original'),
('113.51.c.13.A',3,'The griot in West African tradition was what?','["A soldier", "A farmer", "A merchant", "A storyteller and keeper of history"]'::jsonb,3,'Oral traditions preserved history.','original'),
('113.51.c.13.A',3,'Call-and-response in African and African American music means what?','["A leader sings or speaks and the group answers", "A silent prayer", "A written score", "A solo only"]'::jsonb,0,'It appears in spirituals and gospel.','original'),
('113.51.c.13.B',3,'Spirituals sung by enslaved people often did what?','["Were written by planters", "Expressed faith and sometimes carried coded messages about freedom", "Praised slavery", "Were forbidden everywhere"]'::jsonb,1,'They shaped later music.','original'),
('113.51.c.13.B',3,'Which folktales preserved African storytelling traditions among the enslaved?','["Roman fables", "Norse sagas", "Trickster stories such as Brer Rabbit", "Greek myths only"]'::jsonb,2,'Stories carried wisdom and resistance.','original'),
('113.51.c.13.D',3,'Blues music developed in which region in the late 1800s?','["New England", "The Rocky Mountains", "The Pacific Northwest", "The Mississippi Delta"]'::jsonb,3,'It grew from work songs and spirituals.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Social Studies' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
